  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alabama received $11.9B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $8.5B, making Defense the dominant buyer in the state. Total award count in Alabama reached 85,038, with an average award size of $140K. Obligations fell 34.5% year over year. Annual data show fiscal obligations moved from $13.1B in FY21 to $18.1B in FY25, before registering $11.9B in FY26 to date. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest industry by obligations at $3.4B. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing follows with $2B. The top vendors include THE BOEING COMPANY at $1.2B, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $1.1B, and DYNETICS, INC. at $1B. This snapshot covers contract obligations and reflects fiscal year to date totals that are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting activity in Alabama changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 34.5% year over year. Fiscal totals progressed from $13.1B in FY21 to $18.1B in FY25, then registered $11.9B in FY26 to date. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $140K across 85,038 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal spending in Alabama?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $8.5B, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration at $1.8B. THE BOEING COMPANY, LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION, and DYNETICS, INC. are the top three vendors at $1.2B, $1.1B, and $1B respectively. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) leads industries at $3.4B, with Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $2B."
      }
    ]
  },
